# Direct runtime dependencies for src/ (the packaged backend), loosely
# bounded to a compatible major/minor range - not exact pins. This is the
# file to edit when adding/removing/rebounding a dependency; requirements/
# base.txt is the generated lock file (this file's resolved closure, with
# transitive dependencies included and everything exactly pinned) that
# pyproject.toml and CI actually install from.
#
# To regenerate base.txt after editing this file: install this file's
# contents into a clean virtual environment, then `pip freeze` that
# environment into base.txt. (No pip-tools/uv dependency assumed - a plain
# venv + pip freeze is sufficient for this project's dependency count.)
#
# research_tools/streamlit_ui/ has its own separate requirements.txt - it is
# not part of this package and is not installed by `pip install -e .`.

